            "public_requirement": "Two transistor-level input TIA branches with DC-overload cancellation must accept inp and inn and preserve the specified input bias and overload behavior.",
            "electrical_reason": "Each input has a common-base HBT input device and HBT cascode/load path into an emitter-follower output. The two low-frequency differential sensing pairs compare tiaefp/tiaefn against vref; their reference-side collectors drive HBT followers and filtered gdc_p/gdc_n gates, which control NMOS shunts from inp/inn to ground. This is an active DC sink-control path rather than an RF bypass, while the main input-to-TIA paths remain transistor-connected. The nominal and overload operating-point measurements also show balanced inputs and bounded overload voltages."
