            "public_requirement": "Two transistor-level gain-controlled RF stages must provide monotonic gain control and the specified transimpedance, bandwidth, and group delay.",
            "electrical_reason": "VGA1 and VGA2 are separate differential HBT stages with shared tail nodes and resistive emitter degeneration, inductive/resistive collector loads, and HBT emitter-follower outputs. In each stage an NMOS controlled by gc changes tail-node current, so gc is physically coupled to both RF gain mechanisms. The measured AC sweep reports a nonzero 1.685 dB monotonic gain span and 58.8 GHz bandwidth, corroborating that the two-stage gc-controlled signal path is active; the gain-target misses are sizing/performance misses rather than a missing stage."
