            "public_requirement": "The required TIA, two RF stages, output buffer, detector, AGC, and selector must form a complete receiver whose finalp and finaln outputs meet the nominal, overload, power, and PAM4 requirements.",
            "electrical_reason": "A physical forward signal path exists from inp/inn through the TIA followers, both RF stages, AC-coupled buffer inputs, active output buffer, and symmetric finalp/finaln delay network; detector taps and a nominal detector-to-selector control chain are also wired. Nevertheless, the required closed detector-responsive AGC function is materially nonfunctional: detp/detn reach agcs, but the saturated xqagp/xqagn stage does not create a usable agc control voltage, so automatic selection merely forwards an externally imposed agc rather than receiver-derived control to gc and the VGA tail NMOS devices. Consequently the required blocks do not form a coherently operating complete AGC receiver, and the PAM4 runs also abort before demonstrating complete-receiver operation."
          }
